\dfrac{\left(1+\dfrac{s}{\omega_0}\right)}{s}\] Put \(s=j\omega\), \[G(j\omega)=K\frac{(1+\dfrac{j\omega}{\omega_0})}{(j\omega)}\] For \(\omega&gt;&gt;\omega_0\), both zero and pole are activated. \[G(j\omega)\approx K\frac{(\dfrac{j\omega}{\omega_0})}{(j\omega)}\] Let, \(\omega = \omega_0\), \[G(j\omega_0)\approx K\frac{(\dfrac{j\omega_0}{\omega_0})}{(j\omega_0)}\] \[G(j\omega_0)\approx K\frac{1}{\omega_0}\] Consider magnitude in dB, \[20\log{G(j\omega)}\approx 20\log{\frac{K}{\omega_0}}\] From the plot, \(\omega &gt; \omega_0\) the high-frequency asymptote is \(0\,\text{dB}\). \[20\log\left(\frac{K}{\omega_0}\right)=0\] \[\frac{K}{\omega_0}=1\] \[K=\omega_0\] Hence, \[G(s)=
\omega_0
