The reactance relay characteristic is \[X \leq 1\,\Omega\] The impedance seen by the relay is \[Z = R + jX\] Admittance is given by \[Y = \frac{1}{Z} = G + jB\] Therefore, \[G + jB
=
\frac{1}{R + jX}
=
\frac{R - jX}{R^2 + X^2}\] Comparing real and imaginary parts, \[G = \frac{R}{R^2 + X^2}\] \[B = -\frac{X}{R^2 + X^2}\] Given relay characteristic: \[X = 1\] Substituting into the expression for \(B\), \[B = -\frac{1}{R^2 + 1}\] and \[G = \frac{R}{R^2 + 1}\] Now, \[\begin{aligned}
G^2 + \left(B + \frac{1}{2}\right)^2
&amp;=
\frac{R^2}{(R^2+1)^2}
+
\left(
-\frac{1}{R^2+1}
+
\frac{1}{2}
\right)^2
\\[6pt]
&amp;=
\frac{R^2}{(R^2+1)^2}
+
\left(
\frac{R^2-1}{2(R^2+1)}
\right)^2
\\[6pt]
&amp;=
\frac{4R^2 + (R^2-1)^2}{4(R^2+1)^2}
\\[6pt]
&amp;=
\frac{R^4 + 2R^2 + 1}{4(R^2+1)^2}
\\[6pt]
&amp;=
\frac{(R^2+1)^2}{4(R^2+1)^2}
\\[6pt]
&amp;=
\frac{1}{4}
\end{aligned}\] Hence, the characteristic is \[G^2 + \left(B + \frac{1}{2}\right)^2 = \frac{1}{4}\] Since the relay operates for \[X \leq 1\] the operating region is \[G^2 + \left(B + \frac{1}{2}\right)^2 \geq \frac{1}{4}\] Therefore, the correct option is \[\boxed{\text{(A)} \ G^2 + \left(B + \frac{1}{2}\right)^2 \geq \frac{1}{4}}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>Reactance relay characteristic is specified in the impedance plane.</li><li>Transformation from impedance plane to admittance plane converts straight-line characteristics into circles.</li></ul></div> <div class="sol-block sol-mistakes"><div class="sol-block-title">Mistakes to avoid</div><ul><li>Do not forget the negative sign in susceptance: \[B = -\frac{X}{R^2+X^2}\]</li><li>Do not confuse impedance-plane characteristics with admittance-plane characteristics.</li></ul></div>

